# One line-ending convention in the repository, whoever checks it out.
#
# This repo is worked on by more than one agent from more than one platform:
# Claude Code runs on Windows (core.autocrlf=true), Codex runs in a Linux
# container. CRLF had been committed into the blobs, so a Linux agent rewriting
# a file with LF produced a diff touching every line of it. Two agents editing
# different functions in the same file would then conflict on every line of the
# file rather than on the lines they actually changed.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` stores LF in the repository and checks LF out everywhere,
# which is what Node, Next.js, and every tool in this project expect anyway.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated: keep it out of review diffs, but still merge it normally.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true

# Binary — never touch these bytes.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.webp   binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.gz     binary
*.zip    binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.xls    binary
